# sin-e-phile — environment variable template
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is git-ignored and must NEVER be committed.
# Every value here is a PLACEHOLDER. Never commit a real key to this file.
#
# The application is fully functional with NONE of these set. See ADR-0013:
# the offline catalogue (IMDb + MovieLens) provides titles, years, cast, crew,
# ratings, semantic search and recommendations with no key of any kind.
# Everything below unlocks enrichment, not core function.

# ── Optional: artwork and rich detail (SPEC.md §14, ADR-0013) ─────────
# Unlocks posters, backdrops, cast headshots, richer synopses.
# Free, instant, non-commercial: themoviedb.org -> Settings -> API
TMDB_API_KEY=

# ── Optional: higher-quality artwork (SPEC.md §14) ────────────────────
# Logos, clearart, backgrounds. Free personal key.
FANART_TV_API_KEY=

# ── Optional: hash-matched subtitles (SPEC.md §14, Phase 10) ──────────
# Heavily rate-limited on the free tier; the pipeline treats the daily
# quota as a scarce budgeted resource. Embedded tracks are the default path.
OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY=
OPENSUBTITLES_USERNAME=
OPENSUBTITLES_PASSWORD=

# ── Optional: watch history sync (SPEC.md §14, Phase 19) ──────────────
TRAKT_CLIENT_ID=
TRAKT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── No key required ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AniList  - public GraphQL, no key
# Jikan    - public REST, no key, rate-limited
# IMDb datasets, MovieLens - free downloads, no account
